  "executive_briefing": "As of late July 2026, the digital asset ecosystem reflects a pivotal transition toward institutional integration, cross-chain interoperability, and formal market structure regulation. The release of the Senate's 600-page CLARITY Act text marks a critical legislative juncture, setting ethical and operational boundaries for digital assets ahead of the impending congressional recess. Simultaneously, cross-chain liquidity is shifting away from vulnerable wrapped token bridges toward native non-custodial settlement protocols like THORChain, Symbiosis, and deBridge. While Ethereum sustains strong EVM execution dominance and developer mindshare via Layer-2 networks, emerging Bitcoin smart contract capabilities and native programmability present structural competition. Furthermore, institutional Bitcoin participation is maturing from speculative spot ETF inflows into strategic treasury allocations and sovereign reserve management.",
